sweet ufs: dump the log ring without the lock from the watchdog

bp19 and bp20 both stop at ~8.5 s with the console gone: `sweetfb_noconsole`
pauses kernel output when the GUI takes the framebuffer, so from then on the
only record is the 4 MiB ring, and the thread that copies it out needs the
very lock that is stuck (both boots showed `fage` growing in a boot that
reached "Early boot complete").

`sweet_ufs_emergency_dump()` writes the ring the way the flusher does but
takes no lock, and refuses when a command was issued less than 10 s ago
(then one may still be in flight).  The modem watchdog, which is already
independent of the modem and GLINK threads, calls it before it writes the
BCB, so a wedged boot now leaves a readable log in the partition the host
can pull from recovery.
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -148,6 +148,8 @@
